  title: What Fell to Earth
  concept: Mass vs. thrust (thrust-to-weight ratio)
  nasaSource: NASA Glenn Research Center, Beginner's Guide to Rocketry
  body: A rocket only lifts off when thrust is larger than its weight. Every kilogram
    you add needs more thrust to carry it.
